From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:51:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 030/143] dts: opi4a: CMA 64MB pinned at 0x43000000-0x48000000
 (real DE aperture)

Boot 2 left the board half-dead: with alloc-ranges up to 0x70000000 the CMA
landed at 0x60000000, outside the DE aperture (the X96Q patch documents
0x43000000 reachable and 0x4b100000 NOT). Fetch outside aperture =
interconnect hang. Strict window per the tested layout, 64MB is enough for
bring-up without IOMMU.
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts     | 15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index c874851cb..f2a74183b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -602,17 +602,20 @@ hdmi_con_in: endpoint {
 };
 
 /*
- * The DE's DMA (scanout and RCQ pool) only reaches low DRAM; by default the
- * CMA lands high (~0xb9e00000 here) and scanout would read zeros (black).
- * Explicit alloc-ranges to force it low (the original patch relied
- * on its own board's default placement).
+ * The DE's DMA (scanout and RCQ pool) only reaches VERY low DRAM: the original
+ * patch (X96Q, same die) notes that 0x43000000 is reachable but
+ * 0x4b100000 is NOT. With the previous window (up to 0x70000000) the CMA landed
+ * at 0x60000000 -> fetch outside the aperture -> interconnect hang
+ * half-way through boot (boot 2, half-dead board). Strict window, like the
+ * tested layout: 0x43000000-0x48000000 (after the kernel, before bl31),
+ * 64MB (enough for the bring-up's dumb buffers/fbcon).
  */
 &{/reserved-memory} {
 	linux,cma {
 		compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 		reusable;
-		size = <0x0 0x10000000>;
-		alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x30000000>;
+		size = <0x0 0x04000000>;
+		alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x43000000 0x0 0x05000000>;
 		linux,cma-default;
 	};
 };
